    "statements": [
        "NAV stands for net asset value.",
        "Net asset value is a related financial term worth knowing.",
        "The document describes net asset value as a bookkeeping calculation.",
        "Net asset value is calculated by adding up all assets and subtracting all liabilities.",
        "Balance sheet is another useful financial term.",
        "The document states that a public company reports assets and liabilities on a balance sheet.",
        "The document states that the net amount of assets minus liabilities is generally listed at the bottom of a public company balance sheet.",
        "Liquidation is another useful financial term.",
        "The document offers a theoretical interpretation of net asset value as the amount an investor would receive if a company were liquidated instantaneously.",
        "The interpretation of net asset value as proceeds from instantaneous liquidation is explicitly theoretical.",
        "The interpretation of net asset value as proceeds from instantaneous liquidation does not guarantee an actual sale outcome.",
        "The excerpt mentions future value as an important concept.",
        "The excerpt does not explain future value sufficiently to support a definition based on the document."
    ]
}
